      "id": 2,
      "text": "In 1854 Samuel and Maria Williams bought 21,371 acres in the Blue Ridge Mountains for $4,750, founding Skyland Resort.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.nps.gov/shen/learn/historyculture/skyland.htm"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Twelve historic Skyland structures remain, letting visitors glimpse turn‑of‑the‑century life in the original resort setting.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.nps.gov/shen/learn/historyculture/skyland.htm"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The 1911 Massanutten Lodge cabin was recently restored, offering a tour that brings early Skyland Resort forces to life.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
